      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If your roof insurance claim is denied, do not panic. Read your denial letter, request a complete copy of the adjuster\u2019s report, and hire an independent, licensed local roofing contractor for a second inspection. You can formally appeal the decision, request a reinspection, or involve a public adjuster.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Read your denial letter, request a complete copy of the adjuster\u2019s report, and hire an independent, licensed local roofing contractor for a second inspection"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Review and Protect"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Read the letter: Look for the exact reason for the denial and note any deadlines listed for an appeal."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hold off on repairs:\nDo not start major work yet. Cover leaks with a tarp to prevent more damage, but keep the core evidence intact."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get your file: Ask your insurance company for the full adjuster's file, including all photos and notes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Gather Independent Proof"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Second opinion: Hire a reputable local roofing contractor to inspect the roof and document overlooked damage with clear photos."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check local weather:\nCollect official storm reports or hail maps for your area and date of loss."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check past maintenance: Find receipts or records showing your roof was in good condition before the storm."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "File an Appeal and Escalate"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Request a reinspection: Ask your insurer to review the new evidence, and have your independent roofer present during the new visit."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File a state complaint:\nIf you feel you were treated unfairly, file a formal complaint with the Utah Insurance Department."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hire professionals: If the insurer still refuses to pay, consider hiring a public adjuster or a legal expert who handles property insurance disputes."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What was the specific reason\ngiven in your denial letter?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Was the damage caused by hail, wind, or wear and tear?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more targeted advice on how to build your appeal."
      }
    ],
